From: aiden build <build@aiden.local>
Subject: [PATCH] adb: define libzip in adb build (client-only)

The adb client links libzip (libziparchive), but the libzip CMake target
is defined in CMakeLists.fastboot.txt upstream. Our client-only build
only includes CMakeLists.libbase.txt and CMakeLists.adb.txt, so libzip
is never defined and linking fails:

  ld.bfd: cannot find -llibzip

Define the libziparchive static library directly in CMakeLists.adb.txt
(the libziparchive sources are present in the vendored tarball).
libziparchive also needs <gtest/gtest_prod.h>, available in the vendored
BoringSSL's third_party/googletest, so add that include path too.

Aiden-local patch (not from upstream nmeum/android-tools).
---
--- a/vendor/CMakeLists.adb.txt
+++ b/vendor/CMakeLists.adb.txt
@@ -8,6 +8,25 @@
 	core/adb/proto/pairing.proto)

 # No fastdeploy because it requires deployagent.inc
+# Aiden: libzip is defined in CMakeLists.fastboot.txt upstream, but that
+# file is not included in the client-only build. adb links libzip, so
+# define the libziparchive target here. Include boringssl googletest for
+# gtest_prod.h.
+add_library(ziparchive STATIC
+	libziparchive/zip_archive.cc
+	libziparchive/zip_archive_stream_entry.cc
+	libziparchive/zip_cd_entry_map.cc
+	libziparchive/zip_error.cpp
+	libziparchive/zip_writer.cc)
+
+target_compile_definitions(ziparchive PRIVATE -DZLIB_CONST)
+target_include_directories(ziparchive PUBLIC
+	libziparchive/include
+	boringssl/third_party/googletest/include
+	core/include
+	core/liblog/include
+	libbase/include)
+
 add_library(libadb STATIC
 	core/adb/client/adb_client.cpp
 	core/adb/client/adb_install.cpp
@@ -184,7 +203,7 @@
 	libcutils
 	libdiagnoseusb
 	liblog
-	libzip
+	ziparchive
 	crypto
 	ssl
 	${PROTOBUF_LIBRARIES}
